{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9092-1","published":"2026-11-16T03:08:23Z","modified":"2026-11-24T14:52:19.861850898Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110672","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110673","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110675","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110676","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110677","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110678","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110680","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110681","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110682","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110684","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110685"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-110672","CVE-2026-110673","CVE-2026-110675","CVE-2026-110676","CVE-2026-110677","CVE-2026-110678","CVE-2026-110680","CVE-2026-110681","CVE-2026-110682","CVE-2026-110684","CVE-2026-110685","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110672","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110673","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110675","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110676","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110677","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110678","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110680","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110681","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110682","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110684","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-110685"],"summary":"libcpanel-json-xs-perl vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory\nwhen rejecting certain malformed JSON objects. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-110672)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly limit nesting\nwhen decoding tagged values. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-110673)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly validate\nunquoted object keys when processing UTF-8 input. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110675)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled numbers\nwith large exponents when arbitrary precision number support was\nenabled. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause excessive\nmemory and processor consumption, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-110676)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory\nwhen collecting duplicate object key values into arrays. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial\nof service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS\nand Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110677)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly enforce input\nsize limits when parsing JSON incrementally. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-110678)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled memory when\nencoding certain objects with sorted keys. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10.\n(CVE-2026-110680)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled memory when\nparser objects were copied between threads. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to cause applications using Cpanel::JSON::XS to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-110681)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS incorrectly handled top-level\nvalues when parsing JSON incrementally. A remote attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to alter the number and contents of messages interpreted\nby an application by controlling how input was split across reads.\nThis issue only affected Ubuntu 26.10. (CVE-2026-110682)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory\nwhen encoding certain values as strings. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-110684)\n\nIt was discovered that Cpanel::JSON::XS did not properly release memory\nwhen errors occurred while decoding tagged values. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to exhaust memory, resulting in a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-110685)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libcpanel-json-xs-perl","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcpanel-json-xs-perl?arch=source&distro=esm-apps-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.0210-1ubuntu1+esm1"}]}],"versions":["3.0115-1","3.0210-1ubuntu1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libcpanel-json-xs-perl","binary_version":"3.0210-1ubuntu1+esm1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2026-110672","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110673","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110676","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110678","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110681","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110684","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2026-110685","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","source":"SELF","type":"Ubuntu"}]}],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-9092-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libcpane